    "pop": "~6M",
    "area": "~735 km²",
    "sum": "Positioned at the southern tip of the Malay Peninsula, Singapore is a compact island city-state of ~735 km², having expanded its land area by 25% since independence through coastal reclamation. Devoid of natural resources or farmland, the island commands one supreme geographic asset: sitting right at the narrowest 2.8 km shipping funnel of the Strait of Malacca linking the Indian and Pacific Oceans. Founded as a British free port by Sir Stamford Raffles in 1819 and separated from Malaysia in 1965 with no hinterland or domestic water, Singapore began nationhood fighting for survival.\n\nUnder founding Prime Minister Lee Kuan Yew and the People's Action Party (PAP), the multi-ethnic republic built a meritocratic, corruption-free governance model anchored by the rule of law. Leaping from 'Third World to First' in a single generation, Singapore became Asia's premier wealth-management, oil-trading, aviation, and maritime transshipment hub. In 2025–2026 under Prime Minister Lawrence Wong, Singapore deftly balances ties with Washington and Beijing while scaling up its automated Tuas Mega Port and coastal defenses against rising seas.",
