        "Northern Luxembourg lies in the rugged Ardennes hills of the 1944 Battle of the Bulge, while the capital sits atop the sheer Bock cliffs honeycombed with 23 kilometers of rock tunnels (the Casemates). For centuries, these fortifications made Luxembourg a prized stronghold between France and the Rhineland."
