    "pop": "~9.2M",
    "area": "83,900 km²",
    "sum": "Stretching from the snow-capped Eastern Alps in the west to the flat Vienna Basin in the east, Austria is the German-speaking core of the former Austro-Hungarian Empire that once ruled Central Europe. Roughly three-quarters of its land consists of rugged mountains, funneling settlement and trade into the strategic Danube River corridor and the eastern lowlands bordering the Pannonian Plain. Following the Habsburg collapse in 1918 and annexation by Nazi Germany in World War II, Austria regained full sovereignty under the 1955 State Treaty by enshrining permanent military neutrality.\n\nLeveraging its hinge position between Western Europe and the Balkans, Vienna evolved into a premier global capital for multilateral diplomacy, classical culture, and regional banking. In 2025–2026, Austria stands as an affluent EU and Eurozone member powered by precision engineering, year-round tourism, and an ~80% renewable electricity grid, having ended its long reliance on Russian pipeline gas. Key challenges include reviving industrial growth amid high energy costs, demographic aging, and managing Central European migration routes.",
