    "pop": "~10.6M",
    "area": "92,200 km²",
    "sum": "Forming a narrow coastal rectangle along the western rim of the Iberian Peninsula, Portugal is backed by rugged eastern hills along Spain while facing out toward the open Atlantic Ocean. With borders fixed in 1297, it is Europe's oldest continuous nation-state within unchanged frontiers and maintains the world's oldest military alliance (with Britain since 1373) to counterbalance Spain. Hemmed in on land, 15th-century Portuguese navigators pioneered ocean exploration around Africa to Asia and Brazil, forging the first global maritime empire.\n\nToday, this democratic EU, Eurozone, and NATO member commands vast maritime depth across the North Atlantic through its strategic archipelagos of the Azores and Madeira. Entering 2025–2026, Portugal outperforms the Eurozone average while posting rare budget surpluses, fueled by 30 million annual tourists, a vibrant Lisbon tech scene, and an ~85% renewable power grid. Its chief challenges include urban housing affordability, youth emigration, and downstream exposure to Iberian droughts.",
