    "sum": "Tucked inside a deep Y-shaped valley high in the eastern Pyrenees at an average elevation near 2,000 meters, the Principality of Andorra covers 468 km² between France and Spain. Traditionally chartered by Charlemagne as a mountain buffer and formally established by the 1278 Paréage compact, Andorra is ringed by peaks approaching 3,000 meters. Shielded by rugged terrain and balanced guardianship from both neighbors, the microstate has preserved its autonomy for over seven centuries.\n\nInstitutionally, Andorra is the world's only parliamentary Co-Principality whose joint heads of state are the President of France and the Bishop of Urgell in Spain. In 2025–2026, Andorra thrives on over 8 million annual ski and duty-light shopping visitors alongside digital entrepreneurs drawn by a maximum 10% income and corporate tax rate. Its top priority today is advancing its landmark Association Agreement with the European Union while managing housing shortages and warming winters.",
