    "sum": "Enclaved atop Vatican Hill on the west bank of the Tiber River inside the heart of Rome, Vatican City is the world's smallest sovereign state by both area (0.49 km²) and population (~800 residents). For over a millennium until 1870, the Popes ruled the Papal States across central Italy before Italian unification forces captured Rome. Following nearly six decades of standoff, the 1929 Lateran Treaty with Italy established the independent Vatican City State to guarantee the spiritual and diplomatic autonomy of the Holy See.\n\nThough no larger than a city park centered on St. Peter's Basilica, the Vatican wields immense global soft power as the spiritual headquarters for over 1.35 billion Catholics worldwide. In 2025–2026—marked by over 30 million pilgrims for the 2025 Jubilee Year and the election of Pope Leo XIV in May 2025—the Holy See remains a prominent moral voice and diplomatic mediator in global conflicts. Internally, its priorities center on financial transparency reforms and balancing structural budget deficits.",
