    "sum": "Stretching over 1,750 kilometers along the western flank of the Scandinavian Peninsula from the North Sea to the Arctic Barents Sea, Norway is a rugged realm of the Scandinavian Mountains and thousands of deep coastal fjords. Because steep mountains isolated inland valleys, Norwegians have turned toward the sea since the Viking Age—aided by the warm North Atlantic Drift that keeps even far-northern Arctic ports ice-free year-round. After centuries of union with Denmark and Sweden, Norway gained full independence in 1905 and struck North Sea oil in 1969, transforming into one of the richest societies on Earth.\n\nWhile voters twice rejected EU membership to safeguard control over petroleum and fisheries (participating via the EEA and Schengen), Norway has been a founding pillar of NATO since 1949. In 2025–2026, Norway serves as Europe's #1 pipeline gas supplier replacing Russian volumes, manages a $1.8+ trillion Sovereign Wealth Fund, and acts as NATO's Arctic sentinel bordering Russia's Kola Peninsula. Its chief strategic challenges center on defending subsea energy pipelines and navigating the long-term green transition.",
