    "pop": "~10.6M",
    "area": "450,000 km²",
    "sum": "Stretching from the fertile plains of southern Scania to the boreal forests and Arctic tundra of Lapland, Sweden is the largest and most populous of the Nordic nations. Sheltered on the west by the Scandinavian Mountains along Norway and fronting the Baltic Sea to the east, this semi-insulated geography enabled Sweden to stay out of war since 1814. After its 17th-century Imperial Era around the Baltic, Stockholm pursued two centuries of military non-alignment while industrializing rapidly around vast timber, hydropower, and iron-ore resources.\n\nRussia's invasion of Ukraine triggered a historic pivot: in March 2024, Sweden formally joined NATO as its 32nd ally, completing the strategic ring that turned the Baltic Sea into a 'NATO lake.' In 2025–2026, Sweden stands as Northern Europe's foremost industrial, tech, and defense powerhouse—producing Saab Gripen fighters, stealth submarines, 90% of the EU's iron ore, and icons from Volvo and Ericsson to Spotify. Its chief domestic priorities are curbing urban gang crime and expanding nuclear and renewable power for green heavy industry.",
