    "sum": "Known as the 'Land of a Thousand Lakes,' Finland is a boreal landscape of taiga forests and 188,000 lakes, fronting the Baltic gulfs while sharing a 1,340-kilometer eastern border with Russia. Part of Sweden for six centuries before becoming an autonomous Grand Duchy within the Russian Empire in 1809, Finland declared independence in 1917 and preserved its sovereignty through the 1939–1940 Winter War against the Soviet Union. Throughout the Cold War, Helsinki practiced pragmatic neutrality while quietly maintaining a formidable total-defense system.\n\nRussia's invasion of Ukraine prompted a historic reversal: in April 2023, Finland joined NATO as its 31st member—doubling NATO's border with Russia and contributing Western Europe's largest artillery force and an 870,000-strong reserve. In 2025–2026, the world's top-ranked nation on the World Happiness Report has fortified its closed eastern frontier against hybrid migration tactics while excelling in 5G/6G telecoms (Nokia), icebreakers, and clean nuclear-renewable energy. Its chief structural challenges are demographic aging and revitalizing eastern border provinces.",
