        "The rival power centers in Tripoli and Benghazi have turned Libya into a geopolitical chessboard involving Turkish military support in the west and Russian Africa Corps, Emirati, and Egyptian backing for General Haftar in the east. Meanwhile, straight-line southern Saharan borders with Chad, Niger, and Sudan remain porous corridors for Sahelian armed groups and fuel smugglers."
