        "Over four-fifths of the country consists of the hyper-arid Sahara and the shifting sands of the Ténéré Desert, broken only by the rugged Aïr Mountains rising above 2,000 meters near Agadez. Along the southern savanna belt where most citizens live, flat open terrain offers little natural protection across 5,800 km of national borders."
