        "Along its northern frontier with Sudan, the oil-rich Abyei territory remains disputed under UN peacekeeping supervision (UNISFA), while the 2023–2026 Sudanese war has pushed nearly one million refugees and returnees south into South Sudan. Domestically, with fewer than 500 km of paved roads nationwide, state authority struggles to prevent communal cattle-raiding and militia clashes."
