        "Situated at the triple junction of the Red Sea, Gulf of Aden, and East African Rift tectonic plates, the landscape consists of barren black basalt lava fields, salt pans around Lake Assal, and the small Goda mountain massif. Lacking interior agricultural heartlands or strategic depth, over 70% of the national population lives inside the coastal capital of Djibouti City."
