        "With ~850 km of coastline along the Gulf of Aden approaching the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, the natural deep-water harbor of Berbera is Somaliland's crown geopolitical jewel. Backed by a $442 million investment from the UAE's DP World and a modernized highway to the Ethiopian border town of Tog Wajaale, the Berbera Corridor has emerged as a major alternative maritime gateway to Djibouti."
