        "Flanking the supertanker shipping lane through the Mozambique Channel, Madagascar relies on its main eastern port of Toamasina (undergoing a $640 million JICA-backed expansion), the southern mineral port of Ehoala, and the deep natural harbor of Antsiranana (Diego Suarez) in the north. However, the straight eastern seaboard lacks natural shelter and is battered every year from January to April by destructive Indian Ocean cyclones."
