        "Most of CAR's 623,000 km² territory consists of undulating 600–900 m savanna plateaus flanked by the northeastern Bongo Massif, with a sparse population density of just ~9 people/km². Because the capital Bangui sits on the far southern border and unpaved roads wash out for half the year, the central state has never had the capacity to police its vast eastern interior."
