        "Placing the seat of power in Malabo on volcanic Bioko Island (crowned by 3,011 m Pico Basilé) historically insulated the government from mainland rebellions. However, after gunmen in speedboats attacked the presidential palace in Malabo from the sea in 2009, President Obiang ordered the construction of a new administrative capital—Ciudad de la Paz (Oyala)—deep inside the mainland Río Muni rainforest."
