        "Two volcanic islands ~240 km off the coast of Gabon",
        "Surrounded by over 200 km of deep Atlantic waters, the two islands of São Tomé and Príncipe (lying 140 km apart) feature precipitous volcanic peaks cloaked in primary rainforest, topped by Pico de São Tomé (2,024 m). Their most iconic landmark is Pico Cão Grande, a dramatic needle-shaped volcanic plug rising vertically more than 370 meters above the jungle floor in Ôbô National Park."
