        "Sharing 10,481 km of borders with nine neighbors, DR Congo's geography leaves its mineral-rich eastern provinces (North Kivu, South Kivu, Ituri) 2,000 km from Kinshasa's reach but right on the doorstep of Rwanda and Uganda. Over 120 armed groups and the resurgent Rwanda-backed M23 rebellion (which seized vast swathes of North and South Kivu in 2024–2025) have displaced over 7 million people in one of the world's worst humanitarian crises."
