        "As a classic downstream state receiving over half its surface water from western neighbors, Mozambique is vulnerable to upstream droughts and dam releases. Yet inside Tete province on the Zambezi River, Mozambique commands the giant 2,075 MW Cahora Bassa hydroelectric dam—and is advancing the 1,500 MW Mphanda Nkuwa dam—exporting crucial clean power to electricity-starved South Africa."
