        "Northern Saint Vincent is dominated by the active La Soufrière stratovolcano—which erupted explosively in 1902, 1979, and April 2021, blanketing the island in ash and forcing 20,000 evacuations—and a steep central mountain spine. Terrain on the main island is so rugged that opening the country's first jet airport at Argyle in 2017 required leveling entire hills and filling deep river valleys."
