        "Twin Andean cordilleras running down the center of the country form a dramatic volcanic corridor crowned by 6,263 m Mount Chimborazo—whose summit is the farthest point on Earth's surface from the center of the planet (over 2 km farther than Mount Everest due to the equatorial bulge). This formidable barrier between highland political capital Quito (2,850 m) and coastal commercial hub Guayaquil has defined Ecuadorian politics and infrastructure planning for two centuries."
