        "Peru's 2,414 km Pacific coastline is swept by the cold, nutrient-rich Humboldt Current flowing up from Antarctica, sustaining the largest single-species anchovy fishery on Earth. In November 2024, the inauguration of COSCO's $1.3 billion deep-water megaport at Chancay (17.8 m draft, capable of berthing 24,000-TEU ultra-large container ships) transformed Peru into the premier trans-Pacific hub connecting South American commodity exporters directly to Shanghai in 23 days."
