        "Northern rivers (Mamoré, Beni) flow into the Amazon, while southeastern rivers (Pilcomayo, Paraguay) drain into the Paraná–Plata system",
        "Bolivia straddles the continental divide between South America's two great river systems: northern rivers (the Beni, Mamoré, and Madre de Dios) drain northward into the Amazon via Brazil's Madeira River, while southeastern rivers (the Pilcomayo and Paraguay) flow into the Río de la Plata basin. High in the Andes at 3,812 meters above sea level, Lake Titicaca—shared with Peru—serves as the world's highest navigable lake for large vessels."
