        "Surrounded by five neighbors (Brazil, Argentina, Peru, Chile, and Paraguay), Bolivia lost roughly half of its original 1825 territory in 19th- and early-20th-century wars, ceding the rubber-rich Acre region to Brazil in 1903 and most of the Gran Chaco to Paraguay in 1935. Having ratified full membership in Mercosur in 2024 and holding ~23 million tons of lithium at Salar de Uyuni (the northern apex of the \"Lithium Triangle\"), Bolivia now serves as a pivotal bi-oceanic transit link."
