        "Commanding over 6,400 km of coastline and major container and mineral ports at San Antonio, Valparaíso, and Antofagasta, Chile is a quintessential Pacific Rim trading nation anchored in APEC and the CPTPP. In the far south, Chilean territory straddles both shores of the Strait of Magellan, the Beagle Channel, and Cape Horn—controlling the sole natural sea passage between the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans—while Easter Island (Rapa Nui) extends its maritime EEZ deep into Polynesia."
