        "While enjoying peaceful borders with its five South American neighbors inside Mercosur, Argentina maintains an unwavering constitutional claim to the UK-administered Falkland Islands (Islas Malvinas) and South Georgia following the 1982 South Atlantic conflict. Internally, Neuquén province hosts the giant Vaca Muerta formation (#2 globally in shale gas and #4 in shale oil reserves), while the northwestern provinces of Jujuy, Salta, and Catamarca anchor the booming \"Lithium Triangle.\""
