        "Sandwiched between regional heavyweights Brazil and Argentina inside Mercosur, Paraguay has leveraged its low electricity rates and \"Maquila\" duty-free export-assembly regime to attract hundreds of Brazilian auto-parts and textile manufacturers across the border. Diplomatically, Asunción remains the last sovereign state in South America recognizing Taiwan (since 1957), making it a focal point of US–China geopolitical competition in the Southern Cone."
