        "Thanks to its outlying island chains, New Zealand commands a vast maritime Exclusive Economic Zone exceeding 4 million km²—15 times its land area and the ninth-largest on Earth—served by key container ports at Tauranga, Auckland, and Lyttelton. Yet sitting at the very end of global shipping lines (9,000–18,000 km from East Asian, North American, and European markets) imposes a permanent distance penalty on freight logistics."
