    "sum": "Bermuda is Britain's oldest and most populous remaining Overseas Territory, consisting of a fishhook-shaped chain of roughly 180 coral limestone islands perched in isolation in the North Atlantic Ocean about 1,030 km east-southeast of Cape Hatteras, North Carolina. Permanently settled by the English in 1609 after the Virginia Company flagship Sea Venture wrecked on its reefs—an event that inspired Shakespeare's The Tempest—Bermuda established its self-governing parliament in 1620, the third-oldest continuous legislature in the world. Warmed by the nearby Gulf Stream, the archipelago boasts the northernmost coral barrier reef on Earth and served for centuries as the Royal Navy's \"Gibraltar of the West.\"\n\nOver recent decades, this 54-km² island chain has reinvented itself as the \"World Capital of Reinsurance\" alongside London and Zurich, underwriting a massive share of global natural-catastrophe, aviation, and cyber risk. In 2025, Bermuda implemented the OECD's 15% global minimum corporate tax for large multinational enterprises while reforming domestic payroll taxes to maintain its competitive edge. Generating a GDP per capita above $130,000, Bermuda ranks among the wealthiest jurisdictions on the planet.",
