    "pop": "~16K",
    "area": "91 km²",
    "sum": "Anguilla is the northernmost British Overseas Territory in the Leeward Islands of the eastern Caribbean, lying just 8 km north of the Franco-Dutch island of Saint Martin across the Anguilla Channel. Its name—meaning \"eel\" in Romance languages—captures the silhouette of the main island: a flat, low-lying ribbon of coral and limestone stretching 26 km long by no more than 5 km wide. Colonized by English settlers from Saint Kitts in 1650, Anguilla made modern decolonization history in 1967–1969 when islanders staged a popular rebellion to *refuse* independence within a federation with Saint Kitts and Nevis, successfully petitioning London to remain under direct British rule.\n\nIn the 2020s, this quiet territory of 16,000 people struck an extraordinary digital windfall because its assigned country-code internet domain happens to be `.ai`—the universal acronym for Artificial Intelligence. By 2024–2026, surging global demand from tech giants and startups registering `.ai` web addresses has grown to supply 30–40% of the Anguillan government's entire annual budget. Combined with an exclusive boutique tourism model that bars mega-cruise ships and casinos, the domain windfall is financing major airport and public-infrastructure upgrades.",
