        "The three islands form a strategic North-to-South surveillance chain down the South Atlantic: Ascension Island hosts the joint UK–US Wideawake Airfield along with critical GPS ground antennas and European Space Agency rocket-tracking telemetry. During the 1982 Falklands War, Ascension served as the indispensable mid-ocean staging hub for British task force ships and Vulcan bomber refueling missions."
