        "Under the 1998 Nouméa Accord, New Caledonia held three independence referendums in 2018, 2020, and 2021, each rejecting independence (though pro-independence Kanak parties boycotted the 2021 vote during the COVID-19 pandemic). Following the destructive May 2024 riots that caused over €2 billion in damages, historic 2025–2026 accords between Paris and local factions outlined an autonomous \"State of New Caledonia\" with dual citizenship within the French constitution."
